                "organization": "Baraka for Real Estate Development & Investment",
                "biography": "A Visionary Leader in Real Estate & Cultural Innovation\nCurrently serving as Projects Director at Baraka Real Estate Investment & Development, Ebrahim Al Qassab is at the forefront of shaping Jeddah’s future skyline. Since joining in 2022, he has led the development of six landmark projects across hospitality, commercial, lifestyle, residential, entertainment, and cultural sectors. Overseeing a prime land portfolio valued at SAR 890 million, Ebrahim is actively contributing to Baraka’s strategic expansion into Riyadh, spearheading developments rooted in conscious, community-centered living. \nAn Entrepreneurial Force in the Gulf’s Creative Landscape\nIn 2006, Ebrahim launched OTB Creative Concepts—a boutique agency specializing in \ncommunications, PR, events, and interior design. Driven by a passion for mega events, he collaborated with Kuwait’s Amiri Court on some of the country’s most iconic national celebrations, including the grand opening of Sheikh Jaber Al-Ahmad Stadium, the 50th Constitution Anniversary Fireworks, the GCC Summit, and the inauguration of Sheikh Abdullah Al Salem Museum. \nIn 2010, Ebrahim extended his creative footprint by founding The Hub Gallery and Hubs Café—a unique destination blending art, fashion, and food within a restored heritage home in Kuwait. This concept became a cultural haven for both locals and international visitors. Simultaneously, he expanded into Doha by establishing State Media, a creative and branding firm serving the region’s evolving communication needs. \nA Strategic Marketer with Regional Impact\nEbrahim’s career began in the marketing division of Gulf International Bank, where he managed major offshore accounts across the MENA region. In 2002, he joined Marriott International as Regional Executive Manager, leading alliance accounts in Doha and Kuwait. His success in Kuwait included securing strategic contracts in the oil and gas sector, solidifying the group’s market presence in the Gulf",
