                "photoUrl": "https://static.swapcard.com/public/images/30e0413f819443c987dd30afe7faa919.jpeg",
                "organization": "Inaar",
                "biography": "Dr. Ibrahim Alsini brings over 25 years of leadership in tourism, hospitality, and cultural development. He leads INAAR Consultancy, a Saudi-based firm advising government entities and corporates on hospitality strategy, cultural tourism, and food sector transformation—delivering projects that align operational excellence with global benchmarks.\n\nA former Vice President at Saudi Airlines Catering and Dean of the Faculty of Tourism at King Abdulaziz University, Dr. Alsini has played a pivotal role in shaping Saudi Arabia’s tourism and hospitality landscape. He has served as a judge for the Middle East Hotelier Awards and the Saudi Tourism Excellence Awards.\n\nDr. Alsini holds a PhD in Hospitality Management from the University of Surrey and a Proficiency Certificate from Ecole Hôtelière de Lausanne. He also represents The Protocol School of Washington in Saudi Arabia, supporting the advancement of international protocol and corporate etiquette standards across sectors.",
